#. type: Title =
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/editors-note.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Editor’s Note"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/editors-note.adoc:8
msgid ""
"Warmaster Revolution (WMR) is a fan-based 2nd edition of rules for the "
"Warmaster game.  Warmaster stopped being supported by Games Workshop (GW) in "
"2012, yet there are still many players around the world who love this game "
"and are playing it regularly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/editors-note.adoc:13
msgid ""
"WMR first started as a Czech community-based project but has since evolved "
"into a project supported by large parts of the international community. The "
"Warmaster Revolution Rules Committee (WMRRC), consisting of a number of "
"players from around the world, was established to discuss rules issues and "
"potential changes to the army lists."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/editors-note.adoc:20
msgid ""
"The main aim of the WMR rule set is to implement the combat system from "
"Warmaster Ancients – a second generation of the Warmaster rules system. In "
"brief, this means a limited amount of combat rounds within one Combat Phase, "
"among many other small fixes and enhancements. WMR also features a set of "
"optional rules that focus on adding more dynamics to the game. Finally, a "
"number of minor changes have also been introduced into the existing army "
"lists."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/editors-note.adoc:24
msgid ""
"We believe that WMR offers more dynamic, smooth and “realistic” games than "
"the original version. But most importantly it shows, that though not "
"supported by GW any more, the game still lives on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/editors-note.adoc:26
msgid "_Make Wargames, not War!_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/editors-note.adoc:31
msgid ""
"_In honour of Sergei Kushnir and all the fellow wargamers who had to "
"experience real war._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/editors-note.adoc:35
#, no-wrap
msgid "Website editor’s note"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/editors-note.adoc:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "*This is an unofficial website not associated with the Warmaster Rules Committee.*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/editors-note.adoc:43
msgid ""
"Most of the text on this website is copied verbatim from the https://drive."
"google.com/file/d/1E2YTPKjGeF871Bj7aGaSF1uIlV2domk6/view?usp=sharing[WMR "
"Compendium version 2.1.0] and https://drive.google.com/file/d/1jS81OufTxnx-"
"W850E66LboTVSGQEokoN/view?usp=sharing[WMR Armies version 2.26], available "
"from the https://www.wm-revolution.com/articles/download.html[Warmaster "
"Revolution website]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/editors-note.adoc:48
msgid ""
"Changes to improve the text are marked with dotted underlines or coloured "
"highlights.  **These changes do not modify any rules.** Most of the changes "
"rearrange the text in a more logical order, as used in the _Warmaster "
"Ancients_ and _The Battle of Five Armies_ rulebooks (the two books are very "
"similar).  For example, xref:command.adoc#initiative-movement[Initiative "
"movement] is described in the Command phase (where it happens) rather than "
"at the end of the Movement section, and rules on xref:game-values.adoc#line-"
"of-sight[Line of sight] are gathered at the end of Game Values."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/editors-note.adoc:50
msgid ""
"Text similar to _Ancients_ or _Five Armies_ has been used where it is "
"clearer or provides additional clarifications compared to the original."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/editors-note.adoc:52
msgid ""
"In addition, some wording has been changed to align the rules with the xref:"
"questions-and-answers.adoc[official Questions and Answers]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/editors-note.adoc:54
msgid ""
"[.ancients]#Text taken from the _Warmaster Ancients_ rulebook is marked with "
"a pinkish underline or border.#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/editors-note.adoc:55
msgid ""
"[.bo5a]#Text taken from the _Battle of Five Armies_ rulebook is marked with "
"a gold underline or border.#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/editors-note.adoc:56
msgid ""
"[.qa]#Edits made based on the official “Questions and answers” have a green "
"underline.#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/editors-note.adoc:57
msgid ""
"[.edit]#Other edits are marked with a blue underline or border (as seen in "
"this section).#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/editors-note.adoc:59
msgid "The “Highlight” button in the page footer makes these colours brighter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/editors-note.adoc:62
msgid ""
"Minor spelling and grammatical errors have also been corrected.  These "
"corrections are not indicated — some of them are even present in the "
"original rulebooks.  Small changes to adapt the text for a website are also "
"unmarked, for example replacing page references (though see xref:page-"
"numbers.adoc[]) and diagram numbers with hyperlinks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
